  "verdict": {
    "process_verification_rejected_beyond_spec": false,
    "process_verification_caught_rfwr_cases": true,
    "verify_repair_outcome_changed_vs_exp238": true,
    "conclusion": "Process verification added NO rejections beyond explicit spec checks at the process_aware_verify_only gate (0 cases across both models). However, it DID surface right-for-wrong-reasons integrity defects: Qwen=3 cases, Gemma=2 cases. These are cases where official tests pass but process reasoning is contradictory or unsupported (outcome_correct_process_invalid defect). Process feedback in repair prompts contributed to 1 Gemma case converging that did not converge under Exp 238 spec-only repair prompts. Verdict: process verification improved INTEGRITY VISIBILITY (rfwr detection) but did not improve pass@1 OUTCOMES at the gating stage. The process layer is additive for audit/safety use-cases but not for pass@1 lift.",
    "addendum_weak_harness_analysis": {
      "cases_official_pass_pbt_fail": 4,
      "note": "Cases where official harness passes but PBT finds counterexamples represent weak-harness scenarios. Process verification catches a subset of these as outcome_correct_process_invalid defects when the reasoning is also contradictory."
    }
